ople of  the world they betrayed the interests of  the people on paradise itself so their  desire to protect innocent strangers  could lead to the death of everyone they  know and care about on the island and  this is the brilliance of attack on  Titan depending on which perspective you  take almost anyone can be considered  either a traitor or a hero  except for flock of course because flock  is undoubtedly the true hero of the  entire story anyway as we know in the  real world our own world most wars and  conflicts have multiple sides to them  and so depending on which side you're on  you will have a vastly different  perspective on who is the good guy and  who is the bad guy and the same goes for  who is the hero and who is the traitor  with a few notable exceptions like  germany in world war ii where even the  Germans themselves agree that their side  was in the  most real-world conflicts are incredibly  complicated and everyone believes that  their site is right and that the other  side is wrong attack on titan does a  great job of bringing this reality to  life and the story of attack on titan  really forces us to ask ourselves why  the human race continues to turn to  violence and it also forces us to ask  ourselves of why we are so prone to  looking at the world as if things were  just black and white  when in reality things are not so simple  they are usually extremely complicated  and instead of black and white they are  a million shades of gray this uncanny  ability to shine a mirror to our own  world and to our own human nature is one  of the reasons why I love attack on  Titan and I honestly can't wait to see  how this amazing story is going to end  now please feel free to give me your own  perspective on who the real traitors are  down in the comments below there is no  wrong answer since your opinion will be  based on whichever subjective  perspective you choose to take but I  would be curious to hear your opinions  and your reasoning if you enjoyed t