illing will not end and  suffering will not end all the islanders  are going to do is make their world  smaller but Humanity is humanity and  eventually even the people who remain in  this much smaller world will find  reasons to fight each other this is  definitely a powerful statement  depending on your personal view of human  nature  there is an argument to be made that  competition jealousy violence and hatred  are part of human nature  and no matter where you go in the world  these things are always present wherever  human beings are also present even if  all the enemies of the Islanders were  destroyed in an instant the Islanders  will just eventually start fighting  amongst each other because this violence  is part of human nature floc agrees that  Kiyomi is probably right but as long as  everyone knows their place in the world  everything will be fine and yes we all  know that our boy divine King Emperor  flock has a place at the very top of the  world he is truly an exceptional leader  with a stunning hairstyle as flock  continues to share his genius level  leadership philosophy Armin and Kony  suddenly show up on horseback and they  demand to know where Diaz Ouma Beto's  our flock opens the window and asks them  where they have been all this time  but Armin responds that there is no time  to waste they have to go after the cart  and armored Titan right now according to  Armin the two Titans have escaped the  island and they are swimming towards  Marlay the only way for the scouts to  catch them now is to use kiyomi's plane  to find them and they need Kiyomi and  the his room mechanics in order to make  the plane fly this is actually a pretty  good strategy by Armin flock is clearly  obsessed with destroying all potential  enemies of Aaron's plan so if he learns  that he now has a chance to destroy the  cart and armored Titan he will  definitely be tempted to do it he might  even be tempted to go along with Armin's  plan without resorting to any violence  or bloodshed which is exactly what Armin  is hoping for Armin and Connie then rush  off to where the plane is located the  plane is floating on the water next to  one of the piers but it is being guarded  by Samuel and dads both of these guys  are former members of the 104th Training  Corps so Armin and Clooney have known  them for a very long time although to be  perfectly honest these guys are such  minor characters that I honestly kind of  forgot that they even existed  apparently Samuel and das were preparing  to blow up the airplane and Armin and  Kony are shocked when they see the  explosives but Samuel explains that  Armin and Connie are both suspected of  working with the Marlins and the Jaeger  ist's are worried that Armin will try to  use the plane to stop Aaron Armin and  Connie denied that they would ever  betray the island and they claim to  believe that any attempt to stop Aaron  would lead to the destruction of  parodies but das says that even though  he knows Kony and Armin wouldn't betray  the island they are also the type of  people who wouldn't want innocent  civilians to die even if they are the  citizens of enemy nations this is why  the Jaeger ists are suspicious of Armin  and corny they are worried that  compassion for innocent strangers will  get in the way of their loyalty to their  fellow LD ins on the island meanwhile  flock is also skeptical about arm and  story just to be on the safe side flock  decides to start shooting the Hazara  officers if the mechanics are killed  then the plane can never take off but  flock is stopped by Kiyomi who  demonstrates some frickin epic martial  art skills and takes flock down and  disarms him instantly and before flocks  men can shoot Kiyomi Mikasa breaks in  through the window and takes out the  Jaeger ists unfortunately flock uses  this brief moment of confusion to escape  through the window and he goes on to  warn all the jaegers that Mikasa Armin  and Kony have betrayed aldia and that  they must be killed right away and that  is when all hell breaks loose as McGrath  Jean and hanji are forced to shoot a  bunch of Jager ists to save Myka sake  ami and the mechanics Armin's hope for a  bloodless confrontation is dashed in  seconds  das and Samuel then turned on Armin and  Connie and Samuel actually shoots Armin  multiple times as Armin tries to stop  dad's from reattaching the explosives to  the plane  Samuel then turns the gun on Kony  accusing his former calm  of being a traitor but in that precise  moment Reiner and Annie engaged their  Titan transformations and the sudden  explosions distract Samuel  this gives Kony the opportunity to  tackle Samuel to the ground and the two  of them begin wrestling over the gun  Armen who of course has super special  Titan shifter regeneration powers jumps  on - in an attempt to stop him from  blowing up the plane and a struggle  ensues remember that all of these guys  are supposed to be on the same side and  yet here they are fighting each other  and shooting each other how did it get  to this point how did they all get here  that is the burning question in all of  their minds in the end Kony succeeds in  grabbing Samuels gun and he does what he  hoped that he would never have to do he  shoots both das and Samuel in the head  killing them but also saving himself  armin and the airplane in the process  back on the hilltop where levi falco  gabion con point and Jelena are just  chilling and waiting Jelena says  something very meaningful and something  that echos kiyomi's words from earlier  on in the chapter  upon realizing that the attempt to  resolve the situation peacefully has  failed and that all hell is breaking  loose over at the port  Jelena says that violence is the one  thing you can't take away from humanity  and that really does seem to be the  message that the attack on Titan story  wants to teach us human nature clearly  has a violent streak and no matter what  happens we always seem to find a reason  to fight back when the LD ends of the  island were living in isolation and  complete ignorance about the outside  world they still fought they had a  secret police they made inconvenient  people like Aaron's dad disappear and so  on then when the Marlins attacked they  all fought each other and now they are  fighting each other again based on  whether they support or oppose Aaron's  plan and the cycle just keeps repeating  itself and as we know from attack on  titans history this cycle of violence  has been going on for literally  thousands of years and of course it's  not just LD ins the same is the case  with Marlay they complained about being  the victims of the LD n Empire in the  past but in the present they have their  own empire and they have been attacking  and taking over other nations they even  used Titans  their former enemies to help them  destroy these other rival nations and as  you recall even the LD and  restorationist s-- the LD ins on the  continent who had rebelled against  Marlon oppression  quickly began fantasizing about reviving  the LD n Empire and conquering other  nations it wasn't enough for them to  fight for their own rights and freedom  they quickly started thinking of  themselves as superior and they started  fantasizing about dominating other  nations I'm not sure that I personally  buy the idea that all human beings are  violent by Nature  I think that human nature is more  complex than that but I can definitely  see how humanity's history of war and  conflict can lend itself to such a  conclusion finally we arrived at the  question of who is the real traitor in  attack on Titan which of these  characters should we praise as Heroes  and which of them should we condemn as  traitors who here is doing the right  thing and who is betraying their  comrades and even their own ideals as  with most things an attack on Titan it's  all a matter of perspective with Reiner  and Annie it's probably the most simple  they betrayed their comrades of the  104th Training Corps but they did it in  the name of their original mission as  warriors of Marlay they were willing to  betray the friendship of marko and many  others and even though they felt remorse  afterwards  they certainly caused the deaths of  marko and hundreds if not thousands of  other people are they traitors yes I  would say so they betrayed people who  were nice to them and kind to them and  trusted them but the Marlins did it all  to protect their own families back on  the continent they knew that what they  were doing was wrong that is why they  felt guilty afterwards but they still  did it anyway for what they believed  was the greater good Aaron didn't betray  his comrades on the island because he  wants to save the island but you could  definitely argue that Aaron has betrayed  his own ideals from the very beginning  of the story Aaron always wanted to be  free he wanted to explore the world and  he wanted to fight for justice after  losing his own mother to the Titans he  wanted to kill every single Titan so  that no one would ever have to suffer  like he suffered but once he learned the  cruel reality about the outside world  Aaron did essentially the same thing in  labarie oh that the Marlon Warriors did  to him and his family in chigan China  and eventually Aaron decided to destroy  the outside world in order to protect  the island in so doing Aaron betrayed  his childhood ideals instead of  exploring the outside world he decided  to destroy it instead of protecting  humanity from the Titans Aaron is using  the Titans to destroy most of humanity  in that sense Aaron is definitely a  traitor he is a traitor to everything  that he used to believe in we can argue  that Aaron had to make this choice once  the cruel truth about the world was  revealed but the fact remains that Aaron  betrayed his own ideals and what about  Mikasa Armin Levi and the other Scouts  they believe that Aaron's plan is too  extreme and they are willing to team up  with their own former enemies in order  to protect the innocent people of the  world from the rumbling but even though  many of us can sympathize with their  desire to protect millions of innocent  people we still have to recognize that  the scouts are betraying the interests  of the Islanders at least to some extent  for one thing they are willing to kill  their own fellow Islanders the Jaeger  ists in order to protect some complete  strangers they do so reluctantly but  they are still doing it now you can  certainly argue that the Jaeger ists  don't represent the true interests of  the Islanders you can argue that the  Jaeger ists have been led astray by  flock and his fanaticism but you cannot  deny the fact that actually stopping  Aaron could one day bring about  destruction of parodies now that the  rumbling has been initiated the entire  world will see the danger that the  Islanders posed to the other countries  and so if Aaron is somehow defeated and  the rumbling is somehow stopped before  the other nations are destroyed then  paradise will be in grave danger just  think about it the island is now without  its walls without the wall tightens and  technologically it is far behind the  rest of the world this means that if any  country decides that paradise is too  dangerous they could attack the island  and destroy everyone on it pretty easily  and now that the world has seen the  horrors of the rumbling you can bet that  they will be even more scared of the  Islanders and that they will be even  more eager to destroy parodies and  everyone on it  if Armin Mikasa and the other Scouts  have some sort of brilliant plan that  can stop Aaron and protect the island at  the same time then we can argue that  they aren't traitors and that they are  actually doing the right thing but if  they end up stopping Aaron and the  island is attacked by foreign nations as  a result then we have to concede that by  staying true to their moral convictions  about protecting the innocent people of  the world they betrayed the interests of  the people on paradise itself so their  desire to protect innocent strangers  could lead to the death of everyone they  know and care about on the island and  this is the brilliance of attack on  Titan depending on which perspective you  take almost anyone can be considered  either a traitor or a hero  except for flock of course because flock  is undoubtedly the true hero of the  entire story anyway as we know in the  real world our own world most wars and  conflicts have multiple sides to them  and so depending on which side you're on  you will have a vastly different  perspective on who is the good guy and  who is the bad guy and the same goes for  who is the hero and who is the traitor  with a few notable exceptions like  germany in world war ii where even the  Germans themselves agree that their side  was in the  most real-world conflicts are incredibly  complicated and everyone believes that  their site is right and that the other  side is wrong attack on titan does a  great job of bringing this reality to  life and the story of attack on titan  really forces us to ask ourselves why  the human race continues to turn to  violence and it also forces us to ask  ourselves of why we are so prone to  looking at the world as if things were  just black and white  when in reality things are not so simple  they are usually extremely complicated  and instead of black and white they are  a million shades of gray this uncanny  ability to shine a mirror to our own  world and to our own human nature is one  of the reasons why I love attack on  Titan and I honestly can't wait to see  how this amazing story is going to end  now please feel free to give me your own  perspective on who the real traitors are  down in the comments below there is no  wrong answer since your opinion will be  based on whichever subjective  perspective you choose to take but I  would be curious to hear your opinions  and your reasoning if you enjoyed t